# ── Meeting booking → Google Calendar + Meet ────────────────────────────────
# One-time setup by the site owner (see README "Backend: booking & newsletter"):
# 1. console.cloud.google.com → new project → enable "Google Calendar API"
# 2. OAuth consent screen (External, add the owner's Gmail as test user)
# 3. Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web application), add
#    https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground as an authorized redirect URI
# 4. In the OAuth Playground (gear icon → use your own credentials), authorize
#    scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events + calendar.freebusy,
#    exchange for tokens, copy the refresh token below.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# Optional; defaults to the owner's primary calendar
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID=primary

# ── Admin panel (/admin) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Password the editor types into the panel. Panel is fully locked without it.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Fine-grained GitHub personal access token with Contents read/write on the
# site repo only (github.com → Settings → Developer settings → Tokens).
# Publishing commits the article to the repo, which triggers a redeploy.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITHUB_REPO=JamesBaisus/The-Human-Thread
GITHUB_BRANCH=main
